Multivariate Hotelling test for growth comparison (Bonferroni CI´s) 
-------------------------------------------------------------------

     ^hotegf2^  S1 S2 P1 P2 N1 N2 CL


S1 and S2 are the variance-covariance matrices for (three parameter) growth 
	function (von Bertalanffy, Gomperz, Logistic) for each fish population

P1 and P2 are the (three) parameter column vectors for each fish population

N1 and N2 are the corresponding sample sizes

CL is the desired confidence level (i.e. 99)

Description
-----------

This program performs the multivariate test for comparing growth functions 
(von Bertalanffy, Gomperz, Logistic), considering Hotelling's T^2 statistic
(based on Bernard, D.R. 1981. Multivariate analysis as a means of 
comparing growth in fish. Canadian Journal of Fisheries and Aquatic 
Sciences, 38; 223-236). It displays a table with the results.
This is the version with the Bonferroni inequalities for calculating the
confidence intervals according to Headrick, M.R. & F.J. Margraf Jr. 1982, 

Remarks
-------


All seven arguments must be entered in order to perform the test. The 
required matrices may be entered or obtained by nl vbgf, nl gom3, or 
nl log3. 

This program uses corrected expressions from Bernard (1981) which has
several misprints.


Examples
--------

Inputting the matrices by hand:

. ^matrix Sm = (294.74,-0.6018,-32.57\-.6018,.0013,.073\-32.57,.073,4.2296)^

. ^matrix Sf = (1596.18,-1.1895,-91.05\-1.1895,.0009,.0713\-91.0468,.07,5.76)^

. ^matrix Pm=(441.16,.13,-3.36)^

. ^matrix Pf=(505.97,.09,-4.57)^

. ^hotegfun Sm Sf Pm Pf 78 78 99^


Obtaining matrices by nl vbgf

. ^use kimudat.dta^

. ^nl vbgf mbl age if sex==1^

. ^matrix S1 = e(V)^

. ^matrix P1 = e(b)^

. ^display e(N)^
11

. ^nl vbgf mbl age if sex==2^

. ^matrix S2 = e(V)^

. ^matrix P2 = e(b)^

. ^display e(N)^
13

. ^hotegfun S1 S2 P1 P2 86 78 99^



References
----------

   Bernard, D.R. (1981) Multivariate analysis as a means of comparing growth in
        fish. Canadian Journal of Fisheries and Aquatic Sciences, 38; 223-236.
   Headrick, M.R. & F.J. Margraf Jr. 1982, Comment on Multivariate Analysis as 
        a Means of Comparing Growth in Fish. Canadian Journal of Fisheries and 
        Aquatic Sciences, 39(3): 529-530.
